  "correction": "The generic product does not define DRV_ROCKCHIP. Its Rockchip-named backend comes from dumb_driver.c, not the guarded ChromeOS-specific rockchip.c implementation.",
  "conclusion": "Panfrost nodes fail backend matching and enumeration continues to a Rockchip primary card. The generic backend uses standard linear dumb-buffer ioctls supported by mainline Rockchip; no extra allocation-device selector is required. The port ueventd restores AOSP DRM DAC permissions for both app EGL and the in-process mapper; see the device access audit for the required vendor image sync.",
  "updated_utc": "2026-11-04T00:28:25.434102+00:00",
  "permission_correction": "Both render and primary DRM nodes use AOSP 0666 root graphics. Ordinary apps lack a default graphics GID; Mesa EGL opens Panfrost render nodes and the in-process minigbm mapper opens Rockchip primary nodes. system heap uses AOSP 0444 system system; libdmabufheap opens it O_RDONLY.",
